## 4. gRPC / RPC API## Standard Web Request Structure

POST /skins.OrderService/CreateOrder HTTP/1.1
Host: ://target.com
Content-Type: application/grpc-web
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0

[Raw Binary Compressed Bytes / Non-Printable Text Symbols]

## Vulnerabilities & How to Check Them

* Insecure Deserialization:
* The Vulnerability: The server converts incoming byte data streams directly back into live execution code objects before checking permission flags.
   * How to Test: Alter encoded byte streams using localized protocol buffer maps to check if changing variable properties alters execution boundaries or privilege structures.
* Improper Input Validation / Buffer Overflows:
* The Vulnerability: Because gRPC relies heavily on compiled languages like C++ or Go for raw speed, malformed or oversized byte fields can corrupt system memory handlers.
   * How to Test: Send variable field sizes that heavily exceed defined string parameters to evaluate if the endpoint crashes or experiences memory leaks.

